# React Component Standards

## General Rules
- All components are **functional** with hooks — no class components
- No TypeScript — plain `.jsx` files only
- No default export + named export mix — use `export default` only
- No prop-types — rely on clear naming and JSDoc if needed

## Component Template
```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — clean functional component
import { useState } from 'react'

export default function MyWidget({ title, items = [] }) {
  const [active, setActive] = useState(null)
  return (
    <div className="bg-surface-container-lowest border border-outline-variant rounded-xl p-md">
      <h3 className="text-headline-sm font-headline-sm text-on-background">{title}</h3>
      {/* content */}
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Data
- **Static mock data** is defined as `const` arrays/objects at the top of the file, outside the component
- No API calls — data is hardcoded for now
- Config objects (colors per status, etc.) are defined as file-scope `const` maps

```jsx
// ✅ Define data at file scope
const STATUS_CONFIG = {
  'High Risk': { bg: 'bg-error-container', text: 'text-error' },
  'On Track':  { bg: 'bg-emerald-600/10', text: 'text-emerald-600' },
}

export default function MyPage() { ... }
```

## State Patterns
```jsx
// ✅ Filter state
const [filter, setFilter] = useState('All')
const filtered = items.filter(i => filter === 'All' || i.status === filter)

// ✅ Tab state
const [tab, setTab] = useState('overview')

// ✅ Toggle (e.g. rule on/off)
const [rules, setRules] = useState(initialRules)
const toggle = (id) => setRules(prev => prev.map(r => r.id === id ? { ...r, active: !r.active } : r))
```

## Navigation
```jsx
import { useNavigate, NavLink } from 'react-router-dom'

// Imperative navigation (in event handlers)
const navigate = useNavigate()
navigate('/at-risk/1')

// Declarative links (in nav items) — NavLink provides isActive
<NavLink to="/at-risk" className={({ isActive }) => isActive ? 'text-secondary font-bold' : 'text-on-surface-variant'}>
  At-Risk Monitor
</NavLink>
```

## Do / Don't
```jsx
// ❌ BAD — inline styles for colors/spacing
<div style={{ color: '#0058be', padding: '24px' }}>

// ✅ GOOD — Tailwind tokens
<div className="text-secondary p-md">

// ❌ BAD — arbitrary Tailwind values when a token exists
<div className="text-[#0058be] p-[24px]">

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="text-secondary p-md">

// ❌ BAD — div soup without semantic structure
<div><div><div>

// ✅ GOOD — semantic elements
<header>, <nav>, <main>, <aside>, <section>, <ul><li>
```

## Tables
Always use `<table>` with sticky `<thead>`, not flex-based tables. Use `text-data-tabular font-data-tabular` for numeric cells.

## Status Badges
```jsx
const cfg = STATUS_CONFIG[item.status]
<span className={`inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-full text-label-md font-label-md ${cfg.bg} ${cfg.text}`}>
  <span className="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-current" />
  {item.status}
</span>
```
